! E.frr — Tier-2 regional transit AS
!
! Relationships (Gao-Rexford):
!   Provider:  C (10.0.6.1)
!   Peer:      D (10.0.7.1)
!   Customers: N (10.1.9.1), O (10.1.10.1)
!
! E buys transit from tier-1 AS C for global reachability. E peers with D at the
! regional level — both benefit from exchanging each other's customer traffic
! without paying their respective providers for that traffic. E sells transit
! to stub customers N and O.
!
! Money logic:
!   The peer relationship with D is economically attractive: traffic between
!   E's customers (N, O) and D's customers (L, M) flows over the free D-E link
!   instead of going through C (which would cost E money). This is the classic
!   incentive for regional peering.
!
!   E must NOT re-export C's routes to D (its peer), and must NOT re-export D's
!   routes to C (its provider). Either would make E an uncompensated transit.
!
! Local preference:
!   300 = customer-learned  (prefer — generates revenue)
!   200 = peer-learned      (free — use over provider)
!   100 = provider-learned  (costs money — last resort)
!
! Export policy (valley-free):
!   → provider:  own prefix + customer-learned routes only
!   → peer:      own prefix + customer-learned routes only
!   → customers: full table

bgp community-list standard CUSTOMER-ROUTES permit 65001:100
!
ip prefix-list OWN-PREFIX seq 5 permit 10.255.5.1/32
!
route-map FROM-CUSTOMER permit 10
 set community 65001:100
 set local-preference 300
!
route-map FROM-PEER permit 10
 set community 65001:200
 set local-preference 200
!
route-map FROM-PROVIDER permit 10
 set community 65001:300
 set local-preference 100
!
route-map TO-PROVIDER permit 10
 match ip address prefix-list OWN-PREFIX
route-map TO-PROVIDER permit 20
 match community CUSTOMER-ROUTES
route-map TO-PROVIDER deny 30
!
route-map TO-PEER permit 10
 match ip address prefix-list OWN-PREFIX
route-map TO-PEER permit 20
 match community CUSTOMER-ROUTES
route-map TO-PEER deny 30
!
route-map TO-CUSTOMER permit 10
!
router bgp __ASN__
 address-family ipv4 unicast
  ! Provider (buy transit from C for global reachability)
  neighbor 10.0.6.1 route-map FROM-PROVIDER in
  neighbor 10.0.6.1 route-map TO-PROVIDER out
  ! Peer (settlement-free: avoids paying C for D↔E traffic)
  neighbor 10.0.7.1 route-map FROM-PEER in
  neighbor 10.0.7.1 route-map TO-PEER out
  ! Customers (sell transit to them)
  neighbor 10.1.9.1 route-map FROM-CUSTOMER in
  neighbor 10.1.9.1 route-map TO-CUSTOMER out
  neighbor 10.1.10.1 route-map FROM-CUSTOMER in
  neighbor 10.1.10.1 route-map TO-CUSTOMER out
 exit-address-family
!
